From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] web: save_image -web reports a file it could not write

TileGenerator::saveImage ignored lodepng::save_file's result and logged
WEB-0024 "Saved WxH image to <file>" whatever it returned. Into a
directory that does not exist nothing is written and the log still
says it was, so a caller that trusts the log reads a file that is not
there: bazel-orfs's odb-debug MCP server did, and exited.

A failed write is now an error, WEB-0116, with lodepng's reason
("failed to open file for writing"). Not upstreamed; retires at the
//:bump onto an OpenROAD that checks the write.

---
diff --git a/src/web/src/tile_generator.cpp b/src/web/src/tile_generator.cpp
index 7311d801..02b64bc4 100644
--- a/src/web/src/tile_generator.cpp
+++ b/src/web/src/tile_generator.cpp
@@ -6549,7 +6549,14 @@ void TileGenerator::saveImage(const std::string& filename,
   if (png_data.empty()) {
     return;
   }
-  lodepng::save_file(png_data, filename);
+  const unsigned save_error = lodepng::save_file(png_data, filename);
+  if (save_error != 0) {
+    logger_->error(utl::WEB,
+                   116,
+                   "Cannot write image to {}: {}",
+                   filename,
+                   lodepng_error_text(save_error));
+  }
   logger_->info(
       utl::WEB, 24, "Saved {}x{} image to {}", final_w, final_h, filename);
 }
